      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early Sterling boasted grist mills, grain warehouses, and veterinary practices, all thanks to its proximity to the railroads that linked the area to larger markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sterling_ohio",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community’s climate is humid continental, with average annual temperatures around 52°F and about 40 inches of yearly rainfall.",
